ACK on this info as well.  The kernel.org kernels built with gcc-4.6 and
the previously-mentioned makefile edit seem to work fine: currently
running a non-SMP 3.2.0 build on my PWS 433au with no issues as far as I
know :-).  Haven't tried using gcc-4.5 for a kernel build.

Re: the new libc6.1.  *Very* nice to see the absence of certain
functions in /usr/include/alpha-linux-gnu/gnu/stubs.h :-).  Not having
to worry about future udev upgrades (modulo the stock Debian kernel
issues) is nice.

--Bob



